<!--
This is example level data. Basically every game will have some game design data that gets loaded externaly from xml. 
This provides one very simple method of importing the data into the data manager.

the code will create objects with the associated node names in the data manager. Just change and add lines and then call the variables.
-->

<!--
Bonuses:
1 - Ones to Twos
2 - Ones to Threes
3 - Ones to Fours
4 - Ones to Fives
5 - Ones to Sixes
6 - Remove Ones
7 - Remove Ones Columns
8 - Remove Ones Rows
9 - Remove Dice
10 - Radial Dice Removal
//-->

